  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "d6772ecb-9978-44fa-99c5-7f1013b55b83",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Selecting the Top 10 Medical Specialties\n",
    "\n",
    "The original dataset contains many medical specialties with very few samples.\n",
    "\n",
    "Training a multi-class deep learning model on extremely small classes would produce unreliable results.\n",
    "\n",
    "Therefore, we select the 10 most represented specialties. This provides enough training examples for each selected class while keeping the GRU model lightweight and fast to train."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 12,
   "id": "aa2750d8-878c-4363-b7a2-c5a2366ecc9c",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "Selected specialties:\n",
      "['Surgery', 'Radiology', 'General Medicine', 'Urology', 'SOAP / Chart / Progress Notes', 'Neurology', 'Orthopedic', 'Consult - History and Phy.', 'Pediatrics - Neonatal', 'Psychiatry / Psychology']\n",
      "\n",
      "Dataset shape: (1962, 5)\n",
      "\n",
      "Class distribution:\n"
     ]
    },
    {
     "data": {
      "text/plain": [
       "medical_specialty\n",
       "Surgery                          976\n",
       "Radiology                        248\n",
       "General Medicine                 157\n",
       "Urology                          156\n",
       "SOAP / Chart / Progress Notes    144\n",
       "Neurology                         67\n",
       "Orthopedic                        56\n",
       "Consult - History and Phy.        55\n",
       "Pediatrics - Neonatal             52\n",
       "Psychiatry / Psychology           51\n",
       "Name: count, dtype: int64"
      ]
     },
     "metadata": {},
     "output_type": "display_data"
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "TOP_N = 10\n",
    "\n",
    "top_specialties = (\n",
    "    df[\"medical_specialty\"]\n",
    "    .value_counts()\n",
    "    .head(TOP_N)\n",
    "    .index\n",
    ")\n",
    "\n",
    "df_model = df[\n",
    "    df[\"medical_specialty\"].isin(top_specialties)\n",
    "].copy()\n",
    "\n",
    "df_model.reset_index(drop=True, inplace=True)\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"Selected specialties:\")\n",
    "print(top_specialties.tolist())\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"\\nDataset shape:\", df_model.shape)\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"\\nClass distribution:\")\n",
    "display(df_model[\"medical_specialty\"].value_counts())"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 13,
   "id": "a2c7badb-0bac-4094-9ccf-0c1da515d8db",
   "metadata": {},
